                    <h2>Engineering Graphics and Design Lab</h2>
                    <p class="content-text">
                        The Engineering Graphics and Design Lab helps students learn how to represent ideas and objects through drawings. In this lab, students practice creating technical sketches, reading engineering drawings, and developing accurate 2D and 3D models. It builds the fundamental skills required to clearly communicate engineering concepts and prepare designs used in real-world construction and manufacturing activities.
                        The lab is well-equipped with 75 adjustable drawing tables, providing ample space and flexibility for practical hands-on learning.
                    </p>
                    <p class="content-text">List of Experiments</p>
                    <ul class="content-text">
                        <li>Introduction to engineering drawing and orthographic projections.</li>
                        <li>Projection of planes and solids.</li>
                        <li>Sections of regular solids and development of surfaces.</li>
                        <li>Isometric projection.</li>
                        <li>Introduction to computer-aided design.</li>
                    </ul>

